# gpu-lease TEST configuration: the live GPU node, minutes instead of hours.
#
# This is for working through README -> "Verifying a deployment" beside a live
# deployment without touching it -- a separate course tag, database and port.
# Everything about the control plane is exercised for real: launch, readiness,
# peers over IMDS, the reaper, the budget, termination.
#
# It now launches what gpulease.env launches -- g4dn.xlarge on the course AMI,
# ~$0.53/hour/node, so a two-node session runs ~$1.06/hour -- because what is
# worth rehearsing before a GPU assignment is a real GPU node: the driver, the
# boot script's GPU count, nvidia-smi.
#
# The policy section below is tuned for unattended internal testing rather than
# for a checklist run: unlimited starts, NO lease cap, and a 50 node-hour
# budget. That budget is the only thing that ends a forgotten session, and at
# two nodes it is a 25-hour lease worth about $26. Stop what you start.
#
# Drop back to a blank AMI + t3.micro + 8 GB for anything that is only about
# the control plane. None of that cares what the instance type is, and it costs
# a fraction of a cent -- but on stock Ubuntu there is no NVIDIA driver, so the
# boot script's GPU count comes back 0.
#
# Use it by name, which replaces gpulease.env rather than layering onto it.
# Create the database first -- setup.sh is what does that in production, and it
# only ever touches gpulease.env's:
#
#     export GPULEASE_ENV=gpulease.env.test
#     python -m gpulease.db init            # once, per GPULEASE_DB below
#     ./admin.py preflight                  # IAM: see the COURSE note
#     ./admin.py roster test-roster.csv     # mint yourself a token
#     .venv/bin/uvicorn gpulease.api:app --port 8001
#
# then point a CLI at it with GPULEASE_API=http://127.0.0.1:8001. Without the
# init step every admin read fails with `no such table: sessions`.
#
# Do NOT install this as gpulease.env on a host students are using -- the
# settings below are built for fast, cheap, destructive tests.

# --- identity -------------------------------------------------------------
# A SEPARATE COURSE TAG, and the most important line in this file. COURSE is
# the blast radius: every describe, stop and terminate this service performs is
# filtered by it. Sharing a tag with the live deployment would let a test run's
# `admin.py terminate` -- or a deliberately-passed deadline -- destroy real
# students' instances and disks.
#
# The cost of the separate tag is that the lease host's IAM role has to allow
# it. `StringEquals` takes a list, so install the policy with both:
#
#     sed 's/"REPLACE_COURSE_TAG"/["utcs378","utcs378-test"]/' iam-policy.json \
#       > /tmp/gpulease-policy.json
#
# Without that, RunInstances under this config is denied (an
# UnauthorizedOperation, surfaced by `./admin.py preflight`), which is the
# scoping working as designed rather than a bug.
GPULEASE_COURSE=utcs378-test
# Must match the lease host's own region, exactly as in production: the host
# probes port 22 and authorises itself into the student security group by its
# own group id, which is a single-VPC reference.
GPULEASE_REGION=us-west-2

# --- serving --------------------------------------------------------------
# A different port and a different database, so this can run beside a live
# service without either one seeing the other's sessions.
GPULEASE_HOST=127.0.0.1
GPULEASE_PORT=8001
GPULEASE_DB=/tmp/gpulease-test.db

# --- what students get ----------------------------------------------------
# The course AMI, the same one gpulease.env launches: Ubuntu 22.04 with the
# NVIDIA driver and CUDA already baked in, so nvidia-smi answers and the boot
# script's GPU count is real. Blank = latest stock Ubuntu 22.04, which has NO
# driver -- fine for a control-plane-only run on t3.micro, useless on a GPU
# type. Keep this in step with gpulease.env when the course AMI changes.
#
# The id is cached in-process, so restart the service after changing it.
GPULEASE_AMI=ami-0f0876566775515a5

# ~$0.53/hour in us-west-2, so two nodes for the 15-minute lease below is about
# $0.27 a run. Matches gpulease.env, which is the whole point: this is what a
# student's node actually is.
#
# Two things are shared with the live deployment and worth checking before a
# run, because this config does not know the live one exists:
#   - the account's "Running On-Demand G and VT instances" quota is counted in
#     vCPUs and this type is 4 each, so a two-node test takes 8 out of the same
#     pool the live class is drawing on.
#   - capacity for BOTH nodes has to exist in one AZ; EC2 places all of a
#     group's nodes or none, and the next subnet is tried on a capacity error.
#
# t3.micro (~$0.0104/hour, with a blank AMI and ROOT_GB=8) is still the right
# choice for anything that does not need a GPU.
GPULEASE_INSTANCE_TYPE=g4dn.xlarge

# MUST be >= the root snapshot of GPULEASE_AMI: VolumeSize is passed
# explicitly, so anything smaller fails every launch with
# InvalidBlockDeviceMapping. 128 matches gpulease.env and clears the DLAMI
# snapshots with room for a dataset and torch. Drop back to 8 only alongside a
# blank AMI -- that is stock Ubuntu's snapshot size, and it fails every launch
# against this one.
GPULEASE_ROOT_GB=128

# What the boot script exports as CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES and writes as `slots=`
# in the mpirun hostfile. 1 is correct for g4dn.xlarge, which has a single T4 --
# and matches gpulease.env. On t3.micro it is a fiction that keeps those files
# shaped like the real thing to look at.
GPULEASE_GPUS_PER_NODE=1

# 2, deliberately: the multi-node cases (one subnet, peers over IMDS,
# cross-group isolation, partial cluster) are the ones most worth rehearsing,
# and two nodes is what the distributed-training assignment needs.
#
# At g4dn.xlarge this doubles what a test run costs per hour and takes 8 vCPU
# of G quota rather than 4. MAX_SESSION_HOURS below is what bounds it.
GPULEASE_NODES_PER_GROUP=2
GPULEASE_MASTER_PORT=29500

# Blank = every public subnet in the default VPC. Set these if the live
# deployment uses specific subnets and you want the test to launch beside it --
# they must auto-assign public IPs, or readiness never goes green.
GPULEASE_SUBNET_IDS=
GPULEASE_ALLOWED_SSH_CIDRS=0.0.0.0/0

# --- policy: internal testing, not a checklist run -------------------------
GPULEASE_ACTIVE_ASSIGNMENT=test

# Blank on purpose. Checklist item 13 sets this a minute or two ahead to test
# the deadline sweep; leaving a passed deadline in here would mean nothing
# starts and every run looks broken.
GPULEASE_DEADLINE=

# 0 = unlimited starts, so the hour budget is the ration and you can start and
# stop repeatedly without needing `admin.py grant` between attempts.
GPULEASE_MAX_STARTS=0

# 0 = no lease cap, which is what "no reaper deadline" means here. The reaper's
# case (1) still ends a session when expires_at arrives; it is just that
# claim() now sets expires_at from the budget alone, so at 50 node-hours and
# 2 nodes the lease is 25 hours rather than 15 minutes.
#
# Nothing else will stop it. There is no idle watchdog anywhere in this system
# -- deliberately, since students have root on their nodes -- so a session
# nobody stops runs the full 25 hours and bills ~$26 at two g4dn.xlarge. Set
# this back to 0.25 for an unattended run.
GPULEASE_MAX_SESSION_HOURS=0

# 50 node-hours, counted per (group, assignment). At NODES_PER_GROUP=2 that is
# 25 wall-clock hours per group -- "do not get in my way" rather than a ration.
#
# With no lease cap above, this is now the ONLY bound on a session and on the
# bill: 50 x $0.53 = ~$26.50 per group before anything refuses a start.
# `./admin.py budget 1 --hours 0` resets a group that has spent it (the test
# roster's groups are 1 and 2), and it refuses to run while a session is LIVE.
#
# Checklist item 6 -- the budget-capped lease -- needs this temporarily tiny
# instead: 0.05 node-hours is a 90-second lease at 2 nodes, which is what
# proves the budget rather than MAX_SESSION_HOURS is bounding the session.
GPULEASE_GPU_HOUR_QUOTA=50

# 0 = no floor on a lease. The code default is 15 and gpulease.env runs 5, both
# refusing a lease too short to be worth the boot it bills for. Nothing here is
# near the floor at a 50-hour budget; it stays 0 so that checklist item 6's
# deliberately tiny budget still produces a lease instead of an "exhausted".
GPULEASE_MIN_START_MINUTES=0

# --- termination -----------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to configure. Every way a session can end terminates its instances,
# so a checklist run cleans itself up and there is no leftover volume to
# remember to reclaim. The checklist's deadline items confirm exactly that.
#
# That matters more now than it did at t3.micro: these are $0.53/hour nodes
# carrying 128 GB root volumes. `GPULEASE_ENV=gpulease.env.test ./admin.py
# instances` is the check, and `./admin.py terminate` the sweep -- both scoped
# to GPULEASE_COURSE above, which is why that tag is separate.

# --- reaper ---------------------------------------------------------------
# 20s rather than 120s. The reaper interval is the worst-case lag on every
# expiry, and at 120s each of the timing tests means two minutes of waiting.
GPULEASE_REAPER=1
GPULEASE_REAPER_INTERVAL=20
